.TH EXT4FUSE-WRITER 1 "October 2026" "ext4fuse-writer" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ext4fuse-writer \- mount and recover a managed writable ext4 filesystem
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ext4fuse-writer init
.RB ( --image " IMAGE" | --device " DEVICE" )
.I STATE
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B ext4fuse-writer mount
.I STATE MOUNTPOINT
.RB [ --device " DEVICE" ]
.br
.B ext4fuse-writer unmount
.I STATE
.br
.B ext4fuse-writer recover
.I STATE
.RB [ --device " DEVICE" ]
.br
.B ext4fuse-writer status
.I STATE
.RB [ --json ]
.br
.B ext4fuse-writer allocate
.I STATE /VIRTUAL-PATH OFFSET LENGTH
.RB [ --mode " allocate|keep-size|punch" ]
.br
.B ext4fuse-writer doctor
.SH DESCRIPTION
The owner-only foreground writer uses a private durable recovery directory.
Image initialization clones IMAGE into STATE/chain/image.img; the source is unchanged.
Device initialization requires an explicit offline partition and off-device STATE.
No formatting, automatic disk selection or background service is performed.
The write engine remains experimental.
.SH WORKFLOW
Initialize once, mount in one terminal, and unmount from another terminal.
Unmount waits for clean publication and integrity checks; do not unplug first.
Following interruption, detach any stale mount and run recover with retained STATE.
Device mount and recovery always require an explicit matching device node.
Never delete recovery files to bypass an error or edit an active image externally.
Full-volume reads show progress on standard error, followed by hash/metadata
checks. Read progress at 100% does not mean clean publication is complete.
Only successful device unmount prints a safe-disconnect confirmation; other
partitions on the same physical device must also be unused before unplugging.
Ctrl-C retains state and requires recovery; it never declares the device safe.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --recover-journal
Explicitly replay a supported dirty native Linux journal during initialization
(or managed-image mount/recovery). General filesystem damage is refused.
.TP
.B --checkpoint-every N
Retire completed generations after N commits (mount only; default 64; zero disables).
.TP
.B --check-bytes N
Maximum device metadata-check scratch bytes (default 1073741824).
.TP
.B --journal-bytes N
Native journal import budget (default 268435456).
.TP
.B --timeout SECONDS
Unmount completion wait (default 3600; maximum 86400 seconds). A timeout retains
all recovery state and does not stop the writer. Keep the device connected.
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed package version.
.SH FILES
STATE/writer-state records workflow phase. STATE/writer-lock excludes cooperating
workflows. STATE/chain contains the writable image and recovery history for image
mode; STATE/device contains direct-device identity and redo history for device mode.
Keep the whole directory. Status reads metadata only, not current integrity.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, 1 on failure, 2 for invalid usage, 130 on keyboard interruption.
.SH SEE ALSO
The installed share/doc/ext4fuse-writer/WORKFLOW.md describes installation,
permissions, device admission, recovery and engine/platform limits.
